      "nets": ["SDA", "PWM", "SCK", "POT", "TACH", "RST"],
      "observed": "The design includes both an ATtiny45 (U2) and an ATtiny13 (U3), and connects their corresponding GPIO and reset pins directly together on the same nets. Both devices are also connected to +5V and GND; no selection or isolation is shown.",
      "expected": "The specification describes an ATtiny-driven fan controller, implying one controller MCU. If U2 and U3 are alternative device options, the design should provide a way to select one rather than connecting both devices' pins in parallel.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "an ATtiny-driven fan controller"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"10\") (name \"PWM\") ... (node (ref \"U2\") (pin \"6\") (pinfunction \"PB1\") ...) (node (ref \"U3\") (pin \"6\") (pinfunction \"PB1\") ...))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"13\") (name \"SDA\") ... (node (ref \"U2\") (pin \"5\") (pinfunction \"AREF/PB0\") ...) (node (ref \"U3\") (pin \"5\") (pinfunction \"PB0\") ...))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"11\") (name \"RST\") ... (node (ref \"U2\") (pin \"1\") ...) (node (ref \"U3\") (pin \"1\") ...))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"1\") (name \"+5V\") ... (node (ref \"U2\") (pin \"8\") ...) (node (ref \"U3\") (pin \"8\") ...))"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "If both MCUs are populated, their GPIO outputs can contend whenever they are configured to drive different levels, potentially corrupting PWM or other signals and stressing the output drivers. Even when pins are inputs, the duplicate devices add loading and may interfere with intended operation.",
      "confidence": 0.88
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design connects two separately referenced ATtiny devices in parallel across the controller's GPIO and reset nets, despite the specification describing a singular ATtiny-driven controller. Unless one device is intentionally omitted during assembly, this risks output contention and incorrect operation."
}

